    "body": "## Problem\r\nAPI edits at secondary cursors are lost when the same Insert-mode mapping starts completion.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nPreserve insert-span ownership until completion finalizes redo, then replay its tail at each cursor without losing uncaptured text or per-cursor formatting. Cover replacement, cancellation, completion callbacks and undo.\r\n\r\nFixes #42548.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n- Fresh focused regressions on the corrected source: **21 passed**, covering 46 scenarios with undo.\r\n- Fresh full `mcursor_spec.lua`: **180 passed, 1 existing pending**; all 159 pre-existing runnable tests passed.\r\n- Baseline comparison: 3 passed/18 failed focused; 162 passed/18 failed/1 pending full. Reused baseline receipts precede a whitespace-only test wrap and explicit boolean-to-string conversion in a test name; assertions/scenarios are unchanged.\r\n- Fresh checked-in C linter: passed for the three changed C files, with a nonfatal missing-install `syntax.vim` startup warning retained.\r\n- Official pinned Uncrustify 0.83.0 source build: all three changed C files pass `--check`. Its CMake build reports 0.83.0_f; sources match the CI wrapper's release, but compiler/configuration differ.\r\n\r\nLocal tests used LuaJIT in an isolated offline Linux build and a helper overlay omitting diagnostic `--listen`. The full file used cached markdown parser 0.5.3 rather than pinned 0.5.4. Lua wrapping was checked manually, not with StyLua. These local checks do not include PUC Lua 5.1, clang-tidy, the full repository suite or sanitizers.\r\n\r\n## CI correction history\r\nOriginal head [`07f0c9b`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42584/commits/07f0c9bbe02841db393804197c2faa8f5efcb13c) finished with 34 successful checks, 6 skipped and 3 failed: the AI-assistance trailer syntax, Uncrustify indentation, and a PUC Lua test-file load error from formatting a boolean with `%s`. This revision uses the required bare `AI-assisted` token, the formatter's seven-space correction, and explicit `tostring(switch_window)`. Original failures are preserved; local LuaJIT results do not establish a PUC pass. The current check set for the corrected head has 40 successful and 4 skipped hosted checks as of 30 October 2026.\r\n\r\nThe author has reviewed the changes. Ready for review.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-30T14:57:24Z",
